                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5770623f-81ba-3d69-8c45-17500599c8fc",
                        "entry_id": "db3a0a98-77ca-39a8-9e92-5c3bb47d438d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een ondergrondse, meestal horizontaal lopende, al of niet opgezwollen stengel, het is dus geen wortel"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9be0669-f260-440d-9f41-236a063f0684",
                                "sense_id": "5770623f-81ba-3d69-8c45-17500599c8fc",
                                "text": "De Japanse duizendknoop is een exoot, die niet in Nederland thuishoort. De plant is met tuinafval in de natuur terechtgekomen en verdringt andere bloemen en struiken. De duizendknoop vermeerdert zich met dikke wortelstokken, die wegen en gebouwen aantasten. De wortelstokken zijn zeer taai en liggen diep, zodat de duizendknoop bij gewone bestrijding steeds opnieuw blijft opduiken."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "128db204-8664-409b-a8ea-5ab1721ea1bb",
                                "sense_id": "5770623f-81ba-3d69-8c45-17500599c8fc",
                                "text": "Ja, radicchio, dat zou mooi zijn. Uit Treviso ook nog. En zien hoe de wortelstokken van de bitterplant in ijskoud water in de bergbeken worden gewassen. Er zijn ook prachtige zomerfeesten rondom de Italiaanse radicchio."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d31b2410-7356-452e-8f5d-c7c4d307ddd5",
                                "sense_id": "5770623f-81ba-3d69-8c45-17500599c8fc",
                                "text": "Als de bladeren verdorren, worden de wortelstokken uit de grond gehaald. Verwijder de smalle uitlopers, was de wortelstok schoon en droog ze in de zon."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e7101084-bd4a-4df4-825c-54c41a45045d",
                        "source_entry_id": "db3a0a98-77ca-39a8-9e92-5c3bb47d438d",
                        "source_sense_id": "5770623f-81ba-3d69-8c45-17500599c8fc",
                        "target_lang_word": "rhizome",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rhizome",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a78c26c-097e-3664-a972-9a7f0f03247c",
                                        "entry_id": "7572c79f-46f2-3707-8785-7a10c573e6c9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A horizontal, underground stem of some plants that sends out roots and shoots (scions) from its nodes."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "271affda-b259-40ec-9e9d-12a62f2bc3f5",
                                                "sense_id": "1a78c26c-097e-3664-a972-9a7f0f03247c",
                                                "text": "All these species are climbing, briery plants, having long slender roots, which proceed in all directions from a common rootstalk or rhizome."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "08698ad9-bab0-3d7c-8ab8-5ac1feec8368",
                                        "entry_id": "7572c79f-46f2-3707-8785-7a10c573e6c9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A so-called “image of thought” that apprehends multiplicities."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a8822b3-785c-4197-89a5-f98c9ffb7fab",
                                                "sense_id": "08698ad9-bab0-3d7c-8ab8-5ac1feec8368",
                                                "text": "The corpus of Kafka's writing, they argue, is ‘a rhizome, a burrow’ (K 7)—an uncentered and meandering growth like crab grass, a complex, aleatory network of pathways like a rabbit warren. A rhizome, as Deleuze and Guattari explain in Rhizome: an Introduction (1976), is the antithesis of a root-tree structure, or ‘arborescence’, the structural model which has dominated Western thought from Porphyrian trees, to Linnaean taxonomies, to Chomskyan sentence diagrams."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "193b2fa5-43e2-4734-925f-07e9c417899e",
                                                "sense_id": "08698ad9-bab0-3d7c-8ab8-5ac1feec8368",
                                                "text": "Critical theorists have often drawn from Deleuze and Guattari's notion of the rhizome when discussing the potential of the Internet. While the Internet may structurally appear as a rhizome, its day-to-day usage by millions via search engines precludes experiencing the random interconnectedness and potential democratizing function."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
